{"id":"mount-fuji","name":"Mount Fuji","qid":"Q39231","country":"Japan","locality":"Shizuoka Prefecture, Yamanashi Prefecture","lat":"35.360555555","lon":"138.7275","built":"","year":null,"year_text":"","century":"","era":"Natural formations","period":"","date_basis":"","style":"","heritage":"Place of Scenic Beauty; Historic Site of Japan; part of UNESCO World Heritage Site; Special Place of Scenic Beauty","type":"mountain; stratovolcano; active volcano; isolated peak; shintaisan; highest point","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Fuji","text":"Mount Fuji (富士山・富士の山, Fujisan, Fuji no Yama) is an active stratovolcano located on the Japanese island of Honshu, with a summit elevation of 3,776.24 m (12,389 ft 3 in). It is the highest mountain in Japan, the second-highest volcano on any Asian island (after Mount Kerinci on the Indonesian island of Sumatra), and the seventh-highest peak of an island on Earth. Mount Fuji last erupted from 1707 to 1708.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Fuji","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-51f716a09948","w":1200,"h":803,"title":"Kodaki fuji frm shojinko refurb.jpg","o":"gh-51f716a09948.jpg","credit":{"text":"名古屋太郎, (edited by Hannes_24 )","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kodaki_fuji_frm_shojinko_refurb.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-d85a4caad81b","w":1200,"h":800,"title":"Mount Fuji - aerial view - 1394.JPG","o":"gh-d85a4caad81b.jpg","credit":{"text":"XIIIfromTOKYO","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Fuji_-_aerial_view_-_1394.JPG","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-eefd97f01cbf","w":1200,"h":259,"title":"Sommet-Fuji.jpg","o":"gh-eefd97f01cbf.jpg","credit":{"text":"The original uploader was Ririkuku at French Wikipedia .","license":"CC BY 1.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/1.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sommet-Fuji.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"civilization-v--mt-fuji","game":"civilization-v","name":"Mt Fuji","verified":false,"text":"","text_source":"","text_license":"","images":[{"id":"gh-p1751de95b97","w":663,"h":649,"o":"gh-p1751de95b97.png","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Civilization V, © 2K; Aspyr.","source":"https://civilization.fandom.com/wiki/File:Mt._Fuji_(Civ5).jpg","via":"Fandom (civilization)","note":"Fandom upload by ZeroOne on 2010-11-12"}}]},{"id":"civilization-vii--mount-fuji","game":"civilization-vii","name":"Mount Fuji","verified":false,"text":"is a natural wonder in the Civilization games.","text_source":"https://civilization.fandom.com/wiki/Mount_Fuji","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-p53571575ebf","w":1200,"h":675,"o":"gh-p53571575ebf.png","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Civilization VII, © 2K.","source":"https://civilization.fandom.com/wiki/File:Mount_Fuji_in-game_(Civ7).png","via":"Fandom (civilization)","note":"Fandom upload by Jostriker on 2026-06-19"}}]}]}